  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Mobile App**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing the core user interface for the mobile app. My current focus is the `/src/App.tsx` file. I\'m aiming for a minimalist, mobile-optimized single-column layout, ensuring optimal Core Web Vitals and an off-white aesthetic. I\'ll include a detailed visualizer.\n\n\n**Refining the UI/UX**\n\nI\'ve decided on a single-page, single-column layout for the mobile app, opting for a list view of blog posts. Clicking a post will instantly reveal its detailed view, complete with a back button and top progress bar, and easy commenting. A `selectedPostId` will track the current view state. I\'m focusing on \"MINIMAL NEWS\" as the header.\n\n\n**Defining the \"Cohesive News\"**\n\nI\'ve moved on to fleshing out the core features for \"Cohesive News.\" I\'m planning three daily insights of curated, minimalist journalism. Users can filter by category (Design, Performance, Tech Trends) or use keywords. I also plan to showcase our Core Web Vitals optimization with a sleek mobile vitals widget, displaying LCP, INP, and CLS. I\'m also including a clean newsletter signup and an active post view with key meta-data.\n\n\n**Implementing Scroll Tracking**\n\nI\'m now implementing active scroll percentage tracking in React! I plan to integrate a clean markdown body parsed via `<ReactMarkdown>` with custom components. I\'ll also add a comments section, displaying comments and a form for submitting new ones. The form will send a POST request to `/api/posts/:id/comments`, dynamically update the comment list, and provide loading feedback. I\'ll verify correct usage of `react-markdown` in React 19/TS and ensure efficient file reading. I plan client-side fetches via `useEffect`, targeting `GET /api/posts`, `GET /api/posts/:id`, and `GET /api/posts/:id/comments`. I\'ll optimize `src/App.tsx` for token limits.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now implement a beautifully polished, single-column App component in `/src/App.tsx`. It features search capabilities, category-specific filters dynamically mapped with fluid `motion/react` animations, a reading mode with scroll depth progress indicator, real comment interactions with the full-stack `/api` handlers, and a clean newsletter registration experience\342\200\224all under a cozy off-white color palette tailored for mobile Core Web Vitals."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 952494560
    }
  }
}
