  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Implementing Tech Fonts**\n\nI\'ve successfully integrated the requested Stack Sans Notch font, mapping it to a high-performance display font family with Space Grotesk and Share Tech Mono as fallbacks. The font is now loaded in index.css, ensuring compatibility and performance as a starting point.\n\n\n**Designing Ad Banners**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing the visual design for the ad banners. The plan is to strategically place tech-themed placeholder \"Ads\" as sidebars on wide layouts, and as banners/inline cards on mobile for mobile-friendliness. I\'m focusing specifically on the desktop wide layouts. I\'m working on the design for the left sidebar banner, which will be a clean, vertical banner with modern tech aesthetics.\n\n\n**Refining Mobile Responsiveness**\n\nI\'ve adapted the banner implementation for mobile. The vertical sidebars are now elegantly integrated into a horizontal scrolling container or summarized as a clean horizontal banner after the main content stream. This design optimizes mobile user experience while maintaining the intended visual placement. I\'ve begun reviewing the main content container for optimization.\n\n\n**Structuring Layout Columns**\n\nI\'m now integrating the three-column layout for wider screens. I\'ve focused on wrapping the main content with the appropriate HTML structure, using `xl:grid` to define the columns. The left column, initially hidden on smaller screens, will hold the sponsor ad, while the main content takes the center and a right column will be available too.\n\n\n**Developing Ad Design Elements**\n\nI\'m now implementing a new ad design element. I\'ve focused on creating a visually appealing component with retro digital notches, sparkles, and bold typography for a \"NODE CORE \'26\" ad. I\'ve incorporated sub-millisecond API messaging and edge hosting details. I\'m focusing on the overall aesthetic to ensure it\'s attention-grabbing and informative.\n\n\n**Integrating Cloud Features**\n\nI\'ve integrated a new ad design that highlights \"SERVERLESS CLOUDS\" with zero overhead. I\'m focusing on incorporating a prominent \"DEPLOY CORE\" button that links to the target URL. The design also shows real-time stats with bold values for bandwidth and latency. My goal is to create a compelling call to action.\n\n\n**Refining Content Structure**\n\nI\'m now adapting the layout to include sponsored content at the bottom of the main content block for mobile screens. I\'m focusing on ensuring this placement remains consistent and user-friendly by integrating image ad banners within the side or footer. This will maintain a clean aesthetic while also being mobile-friendly, like the other banners. The existing code has also been reviewed for the intended desktop layout.\n\n\n**Designing Ad Banners**\n\nI\'m now implementing a new ad banner design, focusing on a minimal yet impactful aesthetic. It incorporates elements like an \"ADVERT / META.OPTIMIZE\" label and a stylized version indicator, with a subtle border and corner details, all wrapped in a square. The visual focus is on a central V9.0 indicator, and the color scheme uses neutral tones, all designed to be clean and informative.\n\n\n**Developing SEO Widgets**\n\nI\'m now integrating new SEO-focused ad components. I\'ve designed a \"SCHEMA GENERATOR\" widget with JSON-LD metadata and an \"AUDIT RIG\" button. Another component focuses on \"METROLOGY COMPLIANT\" metadata. The goal is to provide these widgets within the tech banner layout.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 11
      nanos: 121624084
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
