    summary: "Yes, both \"Stack\" and \"Sans\" are related to Google Fonts, though in different ways.\n\n\"Stack Sans\" is a specific font family available on Google Fonts. It was designed for Stack Overflow and includes both headline and text styles[1]. Another font called \"Short Stack\" is also available on Google Fonts, characterized as a low-contrast, semi-geometric typeface[2].\n\n\"Sans\" refers to \"sans-serif,\" which is a broad category of typefaces without serifs (the small decorative strokes on the ends of some characters). Many fonts on Google Fonts fall under the sans-serif classification[3]. While \"Sans\" isn\'t a single font name itself, \"Google Sans\" is a distinct brand typeface developed by Google. It is available as a variable font with various styles and weights[4][5][6]. However, \"Google Sans\" is a trademark of Google and is not available under open-source terms like many other fonts in the Google Fonts library[5]. \"Open Sans\" is another well-known humanist sans-serif typeface available on Google Fonts[7]. Other examples of sans-serif typefaces on Google Fonts include DM Sans, Lexend, Chakra Petch, and IBM Plex Sans[3].\n\nSources:\n[1] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEdjYfl9m0lPZI40tLAJy9Nl4j2py_8rgMhnOc8EQKziLgQAvGsachfX-woiTHKFdWy_vifSVUDW6_ShfYMpwycSMZIubk-rF4PtfM1kR13QNzgHnss3sAhcMqxH26t-Yyuwo8qRc9bG4h6xg==)\n[2] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGC8oluhjayLQ4728KjZgcSqtAfQb97oNkYLNGiy5vBnDrxnalEUH10-aBpHD_GOzse7iWoeuEiT15LZovXsp2w1zilWoeq1QsR4_bFsIMAS0pucqVqeb6xw9K3_DIfBTru7tzIkXNl)\n[3] [baselinehq.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEAkWsn6HzFkf8g1gP9ixJK22mIWKVk_lLAkvlmB_vASEno7BtZTLjihjz07t5CdUe-ljKFEEVpzMVuRw5tsaMfX4yvVQwXSQpdnRA3fYHfluk0ii9-qqyqVoYa0D7EcxEVQOGRMkYMCBL-IqRemtNx1S5Gj4QlP502GsniaL0wOpAanzn2z0Zlg-jr5MpDxc23aGMfRNz1bvbzC_2KIt4la5TrJhkhUg==)\n[4] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.