    summary: "Stack Sans is a sans-serif font family known for its clarity, versatility, and distinctive notched details. It was designed by Koto Studio specifically for Stack Overflow, aiming to balance modernist inspiration with innovation[1][2][3][4]. The unique notched detailing is inspired by the building process and serves as a recognizable signature for the typeface[1][2][3][5][4][6].\n\nThe Stack Sans family includes different styles to accommodate various typographic needs:\n\n*   **Stack Sans Notch:** This style emphasizes the distinctive notched cuts, making them more prominent. It is described as bold enough for brand statements and impactful design, turning geometric letterforms into something screen-native and crafted[7][8][5][9][10]. It offers 6 weights, providing flexibility for headings and body text[7].\n*   **Stack Sans Headline:** This style is crafted for headlines and display purposes, allowing for typographic expression at various scales[1][11][12][13][14][15][16]. It also offers 6 weights for diverse applications[11].\n*   **Stack Sans Text:** Designed for body text, this style ensures effective communication at various sizes while maintaining a cohesive appearance with the rest of the family[1][17][3][18][19]. It provides 6 weights for flexibility[17].\n\nStack Sans is licensed under the SIL Open Font License (OFL) v1.1, which allows for free use in various projects including books, posters, artwork, logos, and websites, with no acknowledgment required. However, there are conditions for bundling it in applications or software[1][4][6]. It supports over 91 languages[1] and is available for download on several font platforms[1][2][17][7][11][12][13]. The font family was first released on October 3, 2025, with version 1.000, and includes 4 masters and 12 styles[1][4].\n\nSources:\n[1] [justfreefonts.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF07dpxxodihLPslku35-qHqExe3IyESK3nl4fpKbXkx6Ds8h8uX6XTRXFtTa8ONVAHLC7rG3A