    summary: "Google Fonts can be easily integrated into websites using CSS, primarily through the Google Fonts v2 API, which is often referenced with `css2` in the URL[1][2]. This API supports both standard and variable fonts[2].\n\nThere are two main methods to add Google Fonts to your website:\n\n1.  **Using a `<link>` tag in HTML**: This is generally recommended for better performance. The `<link>` tag is placed within the `<head>` section of your HTML document[1][3][4].\n    \n\nSources:\n[1] [commercebuild.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHlW9M45avOLFpJ3TSav72YiR1D0IwiIfT8B2GCi5LUcxgWwicMsr6VXapdUlp3H2He9ET1vX_lhV0UNSj-K8TuKguTcHnMX-ra0VSpuOnGnexc8evqKsoVCRDaG8gYDSZ0Pi_YbvBLnhQBLe3RXE4c_uRT9FD8Q7jtxKJKjFP_yKXN3LL_-Ck=)\n[2] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHCG7V06rSdhsoqWZZpvuK3USEBWO3gELWbtOhUwoznxOflU9Ac-UY7pmkyPYLlj2IjsS3zjnvqPesKpv8PXc43CMpugf9siatyqpElBKEeGXy1eNEwH0YhV_if1l4CQUdqy64p6mmcGw==)\n[3] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEYl9JU4hbrXSz7yaJWO836AdJ8Hcxc91J4SZgBA4lRXYbrFSvYgriSpwk26YMez4ty1wauLktYB3P1_cYw2kQu8vxHE4AwFEQF6D9Ps2rEDwjFSIW09b2tjK3kv6bJGtTZ_QldX6DhxPOJXUM-8J61dZR8DUUrudB4SgNRWFnNkh8diDZmGAgd80FX8iL8OAhtfUX4MIOfDSBJr9u8sXBXcuA=)\n[4] [youtube.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHryW6gT1QWot2nIEniKXk9Bbs-wH43h4KNAS1b4GRb7IG4sTB8ujYLqo_IvK-I-uILRYGraagf3J1SozJFTtmjcoFlbK9yQVoSq4Woj4mLTQaocRPtOo6ov2dr86gjOTLX6S3tQxk=)\n[5] [geeksforgeeks.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFpJlSYYFFydleiPU293dQODxVsvDK7G5OJAnNIxBWBtPRqsnrMGD1a0nBaV2ivuaItEB1ZA1vgSQWbCzi1cYO4dTCgtD3ZMH5zH4wSgU8PON1ZMLLFMf9QR1K6lQwDdaoqCCpL4U2QMmB7hmX3-w==)\n[6] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFtKYc_viu8r6oadVmId0WQy_waIW5FI6wM0VaUVKAiDaN25SmOb8i9ryJc4o_zDhm48KgWscuXvefkdAKgdb8DvXurg40LmdOXciPpUInEAE_XHHNUpn5-F1b67MP