  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Responsive Design**\n\nI\'m focused on making the side and bottom ad banners responsive. I\'ve started by examining the `/src/App.tsx` file, specifically the container around line 251. I\'m looking at how it currently handles responsiveness across different screen sizes, hoping to identify how to best achieve the desired results.\n\n\n**Adapting Ad Placement**\n\nI\'m now considering how to make the side ad banners responsive, particularly for tablet and mobile screens. Instead of hiding them on non-`xl` screens, my plan is to adapt their placement. On larger screens, they\'ll remain on the sides. On smaller screens, they\'ll stack at the bottom or transform into landscape banners to fit within the linear content flow.\n\n\n**Unifying Banner Systems**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of our ad banners. I\'ve identified four key ads: `banner-left`, `banner-right`, `mobile-sponsor-card`, and `details-inline-ad`. The current logic hides side banners on smaller screens and displays the mobile sponsor card. I\'m exploring a complete system unification, focusing on a dedicated responsive layout that gracefully adapts all banners across different screen sizes.\n\n\n**Implementing Responsive Layouts**\n\nI\'m now implementing the responsive layout changes. The plan involves a bottom section for banners on smaller screens. This section will feature a responsive horizontal grid, adjusting from one to two columns based on screen width. I\'m focusing on the current class lists for `banner-left` and `banner-right` to refactor for this new logic and implement the responsive behavior.\n\n\n**Refactoring Ad Integration**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating responsive ad banners within the listings and detail pages. My current thought is to render them below the main content, specifically after the `<main id=\"main-content\">` tag, and only for screens smaller than `xl`. I\'m considering unifying `mobile-sponsor-card` and `details-inline-ad` into a single, responsive container that can show both sponsor ads in a side-by-side grid on tablet and stacked on mobile. I\'m taking a look at how the ads render to ensure that the change can be done easily.\n\n\n**Designing Responsive Components**\n\nI\'m now designing the `SponsorBanners` component. My goal is a unified system. For screens smaller than `xl`, I\'ll place a bottom horizontal layout at the end of the content. On `xl` screens, the banners will appear in a left-side layout. This responsive design will use a conditional block within the `<main>` column with `xl:hidden flex flex-col md:grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mt-12` to provide a side-by-side grid on tablets and stacked display on mobile.\n\n\n**Investigating Font Discrepancies**\n\nI\'m now investigating the font discrepancies. It seems there\'s a misunderstanding about the specific typeface. The user requested \"Stack Sans Headline,\" but it might not be directly available on Google Fonts under that exact name, or could be a specific branded font. I\'m cross-referencing this with a Google Fonts search, exploring related font families like \"Stack\" or \"Stack Sans\" to find a suitable match or understand if it\'s a proprietary font. I\'m trying to figure out if it\'s a name variation or if the font is elsewhere.\n\n\n"
