  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Font Application**\n\nI\'ve successfully integrated the fonts from Fontsource CDN and implemented a smooth fallback mechanism. My focus now is on ensuring the correct display font is consistently applied across all text elements. I\'m currently verifying the application of base theme variables within the index file to achieve this uniformity.\n\n\n**Verifying Tailwind Integration**\n\nI\'m checking how the `--font-display` variable integrates with Tailwind. It seems I\'ve got a good base definition for the default font stack. Next, I\'m analyzing the responsive ad banners logic in `/src/App.tsx`, specifically looking at how the `banner-left` is rendered within the grid layout to ensure the intended font is consistently applied. I\'m focusing on the impact on the `banner-left` ad unit.\n\n\n**Analyzing Ad Banner Styles**\n\nI\'m now carefully examining the CSS classes applied to the styled ad banner. Specifically, I\'m focusing on the `font-bold` and `text-[9px]` properties within the `[ 01 // HOSTING_NODE ]` section. My goal is to determine if these styles are correctly inheriting the base font settings I\'ve defined, ensuring consistent typography throughout the application. I\'m also checking for any potential style conflicts or overrides that might affect the intended font rendering.\n\n\n**Confirming Font Inheritance**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on a specific component example to verify font inheritance. Specifically, I\'m examining the node compute display with its various text sizes, weights, and styles. My goal is to confirm that the `font-display` class is consistently propagated to all text elements within this particular component. I\'m also ensuring that any custom overrides are not inadvertently conflicting with the defined global font settings.\n\n\n**Validating Style Consistency**\n\nI\'m now diving into specific HTML structures to validate the uniform font application. I\'m focusing on the `METRIC CLS`, `CACHE HIT`, and `NOTCH` e