        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "Google\'s Core Web Vitals (CWV) are the industry standard for measuring real-world user experience on the web. As search algorithms prioritize pages that offer high performance, achieving scores in the \"Good\" range (green) is vital for search engine visibility and user satisfaction."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
        }
        lines {
          text: "Let\'s break down the three primary metrics and explore how we can optimize them:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
        }
        lines {
          text: "### 1. Largest Contentful Paint (LCP)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
        }
        lines {
          text: "LCP measures the time it takes for the primary content of a page to render on the screen. For blogs, the LCP element is almost always the main headline sentence or a featured masthead image."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
        }
        lines {
          text: "*   **How to optimize**: Deliver HTML directly from the server or use high-performance static rendering. Avoid letting the main content wait on heavy JavaScript client hydration."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
        }
        lines {
          text: "*   **Font optimization**: Use modern font-display strategies like `font-display: swap` to prevent \"flash of invisible text\" (FOIT) without stalling the first paint."
