    replacement_chunks {
      replacement_content: "---\nid: minimalist-design-benefits\ntitle: Why Simple Designs Work Best on Phones\ndate: 2026-05-20\ncategory: Design\nauthor: Julian Drake\nexcerpt: Too many buttons, menus, and pop-ups can make a website slow and hard to read. See how simple, clean designs make reading on your phone a joy.\nreadTime: 3 min read\n---\n\nToday, most of us read articles and browse stories on our phones. Yet, many websites are still designed for big desktop monitors, loading endless columns, annoying pop-ups, and complicated sidebar menus.\n\n**Keeping things simple is more than just making a site look pretty\342\200\224it makes it work much better.**\n\nWhen we remove unnecessary visual clutter, we get three major benefits:\n\n1.  **Super-fast loading**: A page with fewer items loads much faster on slow cellular connections or older smartphones.\n2.  **Easy, distraction-free reading**: A single, clean column of text naturally guides your eyes. You won\'t get distracted by blinking ads or complicated side columns.\n3.  **No sudden text movement**: When there are no heavy dynamic widgets loading in the background, the text stays completely still, so you never lose your place.\n\n### The Power of One Column\n\nOn small phone screens, a single vertical column of text is perfect for scrolling with your thumb. Rather than constantly zooming in or jumping between disconnected boxes on the screen, a simple scrolling page feels totally natural and smooth.\n\nBy putting readable letters and comfortable spacing first, reading a news article becomes peaceful and easy to understand.\n"
    }
    diff {
      end_line: 34
      unified_diff {
        lines {
          text: "---"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
