          text: "author: Marcus Thorne"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "excerpt: Why modern engineering teams are returning to simple, lightweight architectures to solve the latency problems of the over-architected cloud era."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
        }
        lines {
          text: "excerpt: In the past, websites became too complex and heavy. Today, programmers are going back to simpler, lightweight designs for a smoother, faster web."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "readTime: 4 min read"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "---"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "Over the pass ten years, the web development sphere underwent an intense wave of centralization. Sites that once required only basic HTML and a stylesheet were transformed into complex distributed microservice systems, complex GraphQL schemas, and massive JavaScript build packs."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
        }
        lines {
          text: "Now, in 2026, the pendulum is swinging back. Engineering teams are discovering that the latency overhead and hosting costs of \"over-architected\" systems often outweigh their perceived benefits."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
        }
        lines {
          text: "### The Shift Back to Simplicity"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
