  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Admin Panel Components**\n\nOkay, I\'m diving into designing the Admin Panel components with a focus on a clean, minimalist aesthetic. Currently, I\'m setting up the logic: if the `currentView` is \"admin\", and the `adminLoggedIn` flag is false, the system should render a login screen. I\'m visualizing a clean, minimalist card with a form that asks for username and password.\n\n\n**Refining Admin Interface**\n\nI\'ve added a highly visible tip banner to ease login, displaying the credentials: `admin` and `zeronews2026`. Now, I\'m focusing on the admin interface itself. When logged in, a top tab bar will present \"Manage Articles\" and \"View Newsletters.\" I\'m also planning a section with a clean list of dynamic posts, including actions like \"Edit\" and \"Delete.\" A \"New Article\" button will unlock the article creation/editing form with all the important fields.\n\n\n**Implementing Admin Panel Structure**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `<AdminPanel>` block in JSX within the ternary switcher in `App.tsx`. I\'m focusing on crafting the structure and applying the necessary Tailwind classes. I\'m building a container with an `id` for easy targeting. Inside, I\'m aiming for a `space-y-8` layout, and adding a border to the section header. The section header shows a lock, and the header text. I\'m building a logout button conditional on being logged in.\n\n\n**Finalizing Logout Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating the logout function. I\'ve styled a \"LEAVE PANEL\" button. When clicked, this calls `setAdminLoggedIn(false)`. This is a crucial step in the interface design, especially for security, which I\'ve prioritized. I\'m satisfied with the current state of the admin panel. I\'m focusing on the component\'s functionality and aesthetics.\n\n\n**Formulating Admin Input Fields**\n\nI\'m now honing in on the login form inputs. I\'m focusing on the user experience by crafting a clean design. I\'m adding `for` attributes and placeholder text. The inputs have styled classes for clarity. I\'ve designed the username and password inputs, ensuring they are both clear, concise, and user-friendly. I\'m working on the responsiveness, and using descriptive labels.\n\n\n**Refining Authentication Feedback**\n\nI\'m now refining the login error feedback. I\'ve integrated a red, italicized message, rendered as a paragraph below the form, should an error occur. This is a crucial addition to the login experience, keeping the interface user-friendly. I\'ve also focused on the button styling and text for clarity.\n\n\n**Structuring Admin Sub-Views**\n\nI\'m now implementing the admin panel\'s sub-views. I\'m building a simple layout using the existing framework. I\'m incorporating tabs for the \"Articles Index,\" and \"Newsletter Management\". I\'m structuring them into buttons, and using conditional class names for a visual indicator of the currently active view.\n\n\n**Crafting \"New Post\" Button**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"WRITE NEW POST\" button. When clicked, it should call `setAdminSubView(\"new\")` and reset the form. I\'m focusing on the component\'s functionality and aesthetics. I\'m building a button with conditional styling for active/inactive views. I\'m building it with the Tailwind classes, and adding an `onClick` event.\n\n\n**Implementing Article Display**\n\nI\'m now building the article display, focusing on visual clarity. I\'m structuring a table with columns for Title, Category, Author, and Actions. I\'m adding a \"Create Post\" button, using the `Plus` icon. I\'m building it with the Tailwind classes, ensuring it is visually distinct and functional. I\'m implementing the display of existing posts.\n\n\n**Refining Article Actions**\n\nI\'m now refining article actions, focusing on user experience and visual feedback. I\'m adding \"Edit\" and \"Delete\" buttons, styled consistently, with icons and tooltips for clarity. I\'m ensuring they\'re clearly distinguishable. The Edit button triggers an edit function. I\'m implementing delete functionality next.\n\n\n**Integrating Newsletter Section**\n\nI\'m now integrating the newsletter signups display, mirroring the article table format. I\'m adding a clear header, and structuring a table to present subscriber data in a clean, readable manner, aiming for consistent UI elements. I\'m prioritizing data display and formatting for user-friendliness.\n\n\n**Refreshing Newsletter Data**\n\nI\'m now refreshing the newsletter email data display. I\'ve added a section header with the number of signups, and a refresh button. A conditional message displays if there are no signups. I\'m dynamically mapping the `newsletterEmails` array, formatting emails within a wrapping div. The data is rendered with clarity.\n\n\n**Adding Article Editor**\n\nNow, I\'m integrating the article editor form. I\'m focusing on the component\'s functionality, and on handling form submissions correctly. I\'m dynamically updating the `adminSubView`. I\'m using a conditional class to render the editor. It is wrapped in a dedicated form element. I\'m focusing on the overall user experience and making sure editing is smooth.\n\n\n**Implementing Article Forms**\n\nI\'m now implementing the article editor form and cancel button. The editor incorporates a clear UI, with a Post ID field that handles dynamic slugs. I\'ve designed the button using the correct classes, to cancel the form and return to the article list.\n\n\n**Implementing Article Editor Fields**\n\nI\'m now incorporating form fields for the article editor, to handle titles. I\'m focusing on the user experience and clear input labels. I\'ve designed the title input field. It requires a title, and placeholders, which are styled for clarity and user-friendliness.\n\n\n**Adding Article Category/Author Fields**\n\nI\'m currently integrating the category and author fields into the article editor. I\'m building a select element for categories, with options for design, speed, and other categories. I\'m also adding a text input for the author\'s name, both styled for visual clarity and user friendliness.\n\n\n**Adding Article Body Fields**\n\nI\'m now integrating the article body input field with a text area. I\'m focusing on user-friendliness by making it responsive, with placeholders and styling to enhance clarity. I am planning on rendering the post body using Markdown. I\'m planning to make the field large and intuitive for input.\n\n\n**Adding Article Reading Fields**\n\nI\'m now integrating the article reading-time form. I\'m focusing on user experience, and on ensuring a descriptive and clear input field. I am designing a field for reading time, with placeholders for a clear example. I\'m prioritizing descriptive input labels.\n\n\n**Integrating Article Input Feedback**\n\nNow, I\'m integrating the article input feedback messages. A success message appears on successful submissions. Error messages, with clear context, are also implemented. I\'m focusing on user-friendliness, and using visual cues to guide the editor. The goal is easy, secure publishing.\n\n\n**Finalizing Post Publishing**\n\nI\'m now putting the finishing touches on the post publishing process. The button states dynamically, displaying \"SAVING\" during submissions. I\'m ensuring both a \"CANCEL\" and \"SAVE\" button for editing. I\'ve designed and refined the button\'s styling and functionality. I\'m focusing on responsiveness and user-friendliness, to ensure seamless publishing.\n\n\n"
