    thinking: "**Considering File Uploads**\n\nI\'ve been exploring dynamic file upload handling in Express. I\'m leaning toward using built-in body parsing to handle uploads. Base64 encoding appears like a viable option, it\'s easy to implement and needs no external libraries. That might work well!\n\n\n**Evaluating API Approach**\n\nI\'ve shifted focus to API implementation for image uploads. I\'m torn between base64 uploads within JSON requests for simplicity, or `multer` for `multipart/form-data` compatibility. The API requires a UI for image management. I will lean towards base64, preserving standard Express JSON middleware without extra dependencies. However, I installed `multer` and `@types/multer` as a dev dependency.\n\n\n**Simplifying Server Uploads**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on a Base64 approach for server-side uploads. The idea of writing directly to an `uploads` directory, using `express.static` to serve files, feels incredibly straightforward. This eliminates the complexities of multipart parsers, which could be problematic. I\'ve updated the server to handle JSON requests with an increased limit, and I\'m ready to create a post endpoint to handle image uploads! The simplicity is remarkable!\n\n\n"
