  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Implementing Blog Post Features**\n\nI\'m now diving into the implementation details for parsing blog posts, specifically looking at how to handle the `tags` field within the frontmatter of these files. Subsequently, I\'m focusing on moderating comments, including the storage method for those comments and also simulating email logs after a comment is posted. I will look at the best way to utilize the `commentsStore` for this.\n\n\n**Defining Comment Moderation Endpoints**\n\nNow, I\'m focusing on defining admin endpoints. I\'m thinking of how to handle comment moderation, setting `approved` to `false` by default, and crafting a helpful UI message like \"pending administrator moderation.\" The administrative API now needs endpoints: `GET /api/admin/comments`, `POST /api/admin/comments/:id/approve` (or PUT), and `DELETE /api/admin/comments/:commentId`. I\'ve realized comment IDs are stored in `commentsStore[id]`, which simplifies the process!\n\n\n**Refining Admin API Implementation**\n\nI\'m now refining the admin API implementation for comment management. I\'ve worked on the `GET /api/admin/comments` endpoint, retrieving all comments with their post IDs. I\'m also implementing the `PUT /api/admin/comments/:id/approve` endpoint for approval, updating the `approved` status in the store, and handling the \"not found\" scenario with a 404 response. I\'ve started the implementation for deleting comments using `DELETE /api/admin/comments/:id`, removing them from the store.\n\n\n**Adding Email Notifications**\n\nI\'ve completed the implementation of the `DELETE /api/admin/comments/:id` endpoint and successfully tested it. Next, I\'m integrating moderator email notifications. Whenever a comment is submitted, I\'m crafting an email notification with relevant details (author, content, and a link to the admin panel) and simulating its delivery, logging it to the `moderatorEmails` array for future monitoring and testing.\n\n\n**Designing Email Log Retrieval**\n\nI\'m now designing the API endpoint, `/api/admin/emails`, to retrieve simulated email logs. Furthermore, I will create an \"EMAIL NOTIFICATIONS\" tab in the admin panel\'s frontend to display these simulated emails visually. This will show all the mock emails to the moderator. Finally, I will tackle image uploads next.\n\n\n**Implementing Image Uploads**\n\nI\'m now implementing the image upload endpoint. I\'ve set up the necessary directory (`uploadsDir`) and ensured it\'s accessible via `/uploads`. I am designing a POST endpoint at `/api/admin/upload-image` and implemented error handling for missing name or data in the request body, invalid base64 data, and sanitation of the filename to avoid injection vulnerabilities. Now I will continue to process the base64 image data.\n\n\n\n**Finalizing Image Handling**\n\nI\'ve completed the image upload endpoint by processing base64 image data, generating a safe filename, writing the image to the designated directory, and returning the image URL. I\'ve also implemented an admin endpoint (`/api/admin/images`) to list all uploaded images, displaying their names, URLs, and upload timestamps, sorting them by upload date in descending order.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now inspect the parsing and retrieval functions in `/server.ts` to accurately incorporate the new `tags` attribute."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 515124965
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
