  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Frontend Features**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got a solid foundation with tag integration in the backend. I\'m moving on to the `/src/App.tsx` file to implement the tagging system for the frontend as requested. This will involve enabling users to filter blog posts using a variety of tags, not just categories.\n\n\n**Implementing Tag Displays**\n\nI\'m now focused on the frontend display and interaction with tags. My plan is to render visually appealing inline tags with subtle styling on each blog post, providing quick filter options. I\'m leaning toward a soft off-white/beige aesthetic that complements the Zero News style. The goal is to allow users to click tags to filter or add them to a multiple-selection tag filter. I\'m considering using a `useState` hook for `selectedTags`.\n\n\n**Refining Tag Interaction**\n\nI\'m currently perfecting the frontend interaction. I\'ve developed a system where users can click tags to toggle them, enabling a multiple-selection filter. A post is displayed only if its category matches the category filter and *all* selected tags are present. I plan to show active tags clearly with an \"x\" badge for removal. This is a very professional filter. I\'m excited about how functional this will be!\n\n\n**Adding Comment Moderation**\n\nI\'m now integrating comment moderation. My primary focus involves implementing an admin interface to approve or reject comments. I\'ll need to expand the admin panel\'s sub-tabs to include \"comments\". I\'ll also add a success message for users submitting comments, indicating pending moderation. I\'m excited about developing this new administration panel.\n\n\n"
