  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Tab Rendering**\n\nI\'ve got a new approach for tab rendering! I\'m thinking we should refactor lines 715-731 to dynamically map content under each tab. The goal is a more elegant solution. The logic for `adminSubView === \"list\"` versus `adminSubView === \"comments\"` will drive the render of either Article listings or Comments.\n\n\n**Expanding Tab Structure**\n\nI am now expanding the tab structure to include new subviews for moderation. Specifically, `adminSubView === \"images\"` will trigger a custom graphics upload panel render, and `adminSubView === \"emails\"` will render a simulated email log view! Also, I will render writer forms for both `adminSubView === \"new\"` or `adminSubView === \"edit\"`.\n\n\n**Refining Image Upload**\n\nI\'m now refining the image upload component. I\'ve focused on the user experience for image selection. I\'ve added clear visual cues for supported file types and size limits. The \"choose image\" button now triggers the file picker, and is disabled during uploads, with the button changing to \'writing\', for a better user experience.\n\n\n**Improving Image Display**\n\nI\'m now focused on refining the display of uploaded images. I\'m adding a conditional rendering block for the image library index, specifically improving the visual display. The styling is now more compact using flexbox, and I\'ve started the use of `aspect-[16/9]` ratio styling for the image previews, making the layout more predictable. I\'m also planning to add delete functionality soon.\n\n\n**Adding Copy Functionality**\n\nI\'m now incorporating a \"copy\" feature for image URLs. I will add a button to allow users to quickly copy image markdown to the clipboard. The user experience is important, so there will be a visual confirmation that the copy was successful, with a 2-second message and transition.\n\n\n**Implementing Delete and Moderate**\n\nI am now implementing delete and moderation functionality within the image library. I\'ve added a delete button, with a trash icon, next to each image, for quick removal. The `comments` subview for the moderation tab has also been fleshed out, and I\'m adding a basic header. The image copy button now shows different text, if copied.\n\n\n**Refreshing Comment Logs**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the comment logs refresh button! I\'ve just integrated the `fetchAllComments` function. I\'ve styled the table rows in the `comments` subview for the moderation tab.\n\n\n**Styling Comment Table**\n\nI\'m now styling the comment logs table rows! I\'m adding dynamic display logic for cases where there are no commenter submission logs available. I\'ve also added styling to the rows themselves, which use a hover state and apply classes for padding, text color, and truncation to handle long content. The table is now much more readable.\n\n\n**Enhancing Comment Approvals**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the comment approval workflow! I\'ve updated the comment table to use status indicators. Approved comments now display a green badge with a check mark, and unapproved comments show a yellow badge, with a dot. I\'m adding a button that will call `handleApproveComment`, for each unapproved comment, which is conditional on the current approval status. This will be critical for the moderation process!\n\n\n\n**Adding Comment Actions**\n\nI\'m now integrating comment actions into the table! I\'ve added \"Approve\" and \"Delete\" buttons to each comment row in the table, to provide moderation capabilities. I\'ve designed the buttons to be visually distinct, using check mark and trash icons respectively. The logic for conditional rendering of \"Approve\" and \"Reject\" buttons is now set up. The table looks great!\n\n\n**Integrating Email Logs**\n\nI\'m now integrating the simulated email logs view! I\'ve added a section for displaying email logs, complete with a refresh button to trigger `fetchEmailLogs`. I\'ve also incorporated logic for handling empty log states, providing a clear message when no emails are present.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will view lines 712 to 820 of `/src/App.tsx` to double check the exact target code blocks to replace."
